//RS //! D-HOTSWAP1 — type-surface stability check for `jet dev` (incl.
//RS //! `jet dev --swap`, D-CLI-DEVSERVE1=A: was `jet serve`).
//RS //!
//RS //! The hot-reload unit is a MODULE. When a resident program's file changes,
//RS //! the watch loop asks this pass whether the edit is *type-stable*: a change
//RS //! that touches only function *bodies* / statements keeps the same type
//RS //! surface and takes the fast swap path; a change to a struct field, an enum
//RS //! variant, or a function signature changes the surface and forces a clean,
//RS //! announced restart (E2210).
//RS //!
//RS //! This is a pure sema walk over the two parsed bundles' declared types — it
//RS //! NEVER asks rustc whether the layout changed (I3: all checking lives in
//RS //! sema). State retention is emitted per canonical `#Persist` binding, so an
//RS //! unrelated module-surface change cannot reset an unchanged value.
//RS 
//RS use crate::Diagnostics::Diagnostic;
//RS use crate::AST::{
//RS     EnumDef, Func, Item, LoadedModule, MigrationOp, ProgramBundle, StructDef, Type,
//RS     VariantPayload,
