//RS /// Compare the type surface of the named module across two bundles and emit
//RS /// the one backend-neutral decision every live adapter consumes.
//RS ///
//RS /// The decision is successful even when the edit is incompatible: an
//RS /// incompatible edit is a normal semantic verdict that carries its restart
//RS /// reason and fresh-state facts. `Err` remains reserved for future semantic
//RS /// failures that prevent a verdict from being produced.
//RS ///
//RS /// `module_name` matches a module by `display` path or import `alias`; if
//RS /// neither bundle has it, the entry module is compared (the common single-file
//RS /// dev case).
//RS pub fn type_stable_decision(
//RS     old: &ProgramBundle,
//RS     new: &ProgramBundle,
